Nx is a build system for JavaScript and TypeScript monorepos, with plugins extending it to any language. It helps you **develop faster** and **keep CI fast** as your codebase scales.

{% youtube src="https://youtu.be/pbAQErStl9o" title="What is Nx?" width="100%" /%}

## Challenges of monorepos

Monorepos have many advantages and are especially useful for AI agents to have more context and tools to make cross-cutting changes. But as teams and codebases grow, monorepos are hard to scale:

- **Slow builds and tests** - Hundreds or thousands of tasks compete for CI resources.
- **Complex task pipelines** - Projects depend on each other, so tasks need to run in the right order, and that's hard to manage by hand.
- **Flaky CI** - Longer pipelines lead to random failures and inconsistent results between local and CI environments.
- **Architectural erosion** - Without clear boundaries, unwanted dependencies creep in and projects become tightly coupled.

## How Nx works

1. **Nx maps your workspace.** It reads your source code, installed dependencies, and TypeScript configuration to build a [project graph](/docs/features/explore-graph) of how your projects connect. [Plugins](/docs/plugin-registry) read the configuration files your tools already have, such as `vite.config.ts`, and [create tasks from them](/docs/features/run-tasks#inferred-tasks), so most projects need no Nx configuration. The same graph lets [module boundary rules](/docs/features/enforce-module-boundaries) block dependencies you don't want.
2. **Each command becomes a task graph.** For `nx build myapp`, Nx uses the project graph and your [task pipeline](/docs/features/run-tasks#defining-a-task-pipeline) to work out which tasks to run and in what order. Tasks that don't depend on each other run in parallel.
3. **Work that's already done is skipped.** Before running a task, Nx hashes its inputs, such as source files, configuration, and dependencies. When the hash matches an earlier run, Nx [replays the cached result](/docs/features/cache-task-results), terminal output and files included.

When `myapp` depends on `ui` and `utils`, `nx build myapp` builds both libraries in parallel, then the app, and replays any build whose inputs haven't changed.

![The project graph becomes a task graph, and each task is a cache hit or a run](../../../assets/getting-started/intro-how-nx-works.svg)

## Start small, grow as needed

Nx is modular. Start with the CLI and add capabilities as your needs grow.

| Component                                  | What It Does                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |
| ------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **Nx Core**                                | Task runner with [local caching](/docs/features/cache-task-results) and [affected commands](/docs/features/ci-features/affected). Works with any tech stack.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |
| [**Nx Plugins**](/docs/plugin-registry)    | Technology-specific automation (generators, auto-configured projects and tasks, dependency detection).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |
| [**Nx Cloud**](/docs/features/ci-features) | [Remote caching](/docs/features/ci-features/remote-cache), [task distribution](/docs/features/ci-features/distribute-task-execution), [task splitting](/docs/kb/split-e2e-tasks), [flaky task retries](/docs/kb/flaky-tasks), and [self-healing CI](/docs/features/ci-features/self-healing-ci). [Try it for free](https://cloud.nx.app/get-started?utm_source=nx-docs&utm_medium=website&utm_campaign=nx-cloud-signup&utm_content=intro-cloud-table). |

